    light_daemon_cannot_serve_pinned_native_exec_2026-11-03, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep7: reproduced the diversion (SIMPLE_BINARY pin bypasses the test daemon by design - light_protocol v2 carries no binary/exec field; the daemon is pinned to its spawning binary). The recorded KEEP decision (already pinned by the sibling lane's merged light_daemon_pinned_bypass_spec) was implemented as the missing client-side half: the SIMPLE_* selector family + diversion logic lived only inside the bare-fn main client with zero unit-spec coverage. Fix (zero behavior change, post-change repro byte-identical): NEW src/app/test_runner_new/binary_override.spl (closed 32-name selector family, pure active-selectors, env wrappers via the env_ops facade; decision-lives-here pattern per daemon_backlog/timeout_budget) + test_runner_client.spl delegates (3 call sites). Spec binary_override_bypass_spec 8/8 PASS; neighbours light_daemon_pinned_bypass 3/3, daemon_backlog_bypass 13/13, light_protocol 6/6, environment_identity 8/8, native_profile 12/12, worker_cache 4/4, validation_gate 1/1, client_timeout_env 7/7, direct_lane_mode 8/8, explicit_binary_precedence 5/5. Residuals: the end-to-end daemon-serve path is Linux-only (daemon_platform_bypass) - a Linux follow-up replays the documented --compiler message check. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/app/test_runner_new/binary_override_bypass_spec.spl prevention=src/app/test_runner_new/binary_override.spl"

